    "slug": "restaurant-pos-software-cost-pakistan",
    "title": "Restaurant POS Software Cost in Pakistan",
    "seoTitle": "Restaurant POS Software Cost in Pakistan: Budget Guide",
    "excerpt": "Compare restaurant POS costs in Pakistan: software, terminals, printers, setup, training and branch scope. See Restrova fee examples and a buying worksheet.",
    "relatedSolution": "restaurant-pos",
    "content": "Restaurant POS cost in Pakistan includes more than a billing-software subscription. Compare software, devices, installation, training, support and any specialist work needed for your service. Restrova's published model is PKR 10,000 onboarding once, then the higher of PKR 5,000 or 1% of monthly sales processed through Restrova. Hardware, taxes, payment charges and other exclusions need confirmation.\n\nThere is no verified market-wide price range in this guide. Use your actual device list and written vendor proposals. The aim is a budget for the cashier, kitchen and closing manager to complete their work, not a quote based only on the word POS.\n\n## Start with the service and device list\n\nRecord the branches, counters and people who need access. List existing computer and receipt-printer models, network arrangements and any payment devices. Identify whether you need kitchen printing, a display, stock controls or direct online orders in the same routine.\n\nFor a café, the practical requirement may be entering drink choices correctly and handing the order to preparation. A takeaway receiving counter and website orders needs to avoid losing one order while handling another. A chain should test branch access and comparable reporting. These differences affect setup work even when two subscription prices look similar.\n\nUse the [restaurant POS workflow](/services/restaurant-pos) to prepare a demonstration with your own menu. Do not buy replacement equipment until compatibility and responsibilities have been confirmed.\n\n## Build an itemized POS budget\n\n| Cost area | What belongs in the comparison | Question before approval |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Onboarding | Menu, branch setup and agreed training | What work and sessions are included? |\n| Recurring software | Subscription or sales-based formula | Which sales, branches and users does it cover? |\n| Devices | Computers, printers and any required peripherals | Can the exact existing models be used? |\n| Site readiness | Network, power arrangements and installation | Who supplies and supports each part? |\n| Operating supplies | Receipt paper and relevant device maintenance | Which costs remain with the restaurant? |\n| Payments and specialist work | Provider charges and explicitly requested integrations | What is demonstrated and quoted separately? |\n| Ongoing support | Training changes, issue handling and updates | What hours, channels and work are agreed? |\n\nUse real supplier quotes for hardware. A low software price does not prove a complete counter setup is affordable, and a larger equipment bundle does not prove your existing devices need replacement.\n\n## Understand Restrova's monthly calculation\n\nThe fee is the higher of PKR 5,000 and 1% of monthly sales processed through Restrova. It is not PKR 5,000 plus 1%. The minimum still applies at zero processed sales; at PKR 500,000, the two amounts are equal.\n\n| Restrova-processed sales in a month | Monthly software fee | Onboarding plus that month |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| PKR 300,000 | PKR 5,000 | PKR 15,000 |\n| PKR 600,000 | PKR 6,000 | PKR 16,000 |\n| PKR 1,000,000 | PKR 10,000 | PKR 20,000 |\n\nThese amounts illustrate the published formula before other charges. They are not per-terminal prices or confirmation of unlimited branch coverage. Agree the branch, user and account scope with Restrova. Check the [current pricing page](/pricing) for the calculator and exclusions.\n\n## Include connected orders in the sales discussion\n\nConsider a hypothetical setup processing PKR 350,000 of counter sales and PKR 250,000 of website sales through Restrova in one month. If both form the agreed billing base, processed sales total PKR 600,000 and the monthly formula gives PKR 6,000. Adding the one-time onboarding fee makes PKR 16,000 for onboarding and that month, before devices or other extras.\n\nDo not calculate a fee from counter sales alone when other channels also belong to the processed-sales base. Equally, do not add an assumed second subscription for the website without a proposal stating it. Agree how cancellations, refunds and adjustments affect the total. Use the [online ordering cost guide](/blog/restaurant-online-ordering-system-cost-pakistan) for channel-specific operating costs.\n\n## Check costly assumptions before signing\n\nAsk the vendor to demonstrate the intended receipt or kitchen-printing arrangement on the actual device models. If an offline mode is essential, test interruption and reconnection, including how records reconcile. A device compatibility claim is different from support for every printer or payment terminal.\n\nList any required marketplace, accounting, fiscal or payment integration by provider and action. Confirm availability and written scope rather than treating a generic integration label as proof. If a required capability remains unresolved, keep its cost and launch dependency open in the comparison.\n\nBring a small inventory example and a cash-delivery example if those workflows matter. Verify [stock management](/services/inventory-management) and [rider reconciliation](/services/delivery-management) separately from entering a bill. Do not assume every specialist stock or payroll function is part of a POS package.\n\n## Budget for switching and training\n\nPlan who prepares menus and opening records, how staff learn corrections and who closes the first shifts. Ask for a sample import or export when moving data, including the supported fields and format. Avoid assuming all records can transfer automatically between systems.\n\nRun a controlled pilot and retain an agreed fallback routine. Count the restaurant's time spent preparing data, training and reviewing differences alongside supplier charges. The [POS-versus-manual-billing guide](/blog/restaurant-pos-vs-manual-billing) helps compare the work involved, while the [general pricing guide](/blog/restaurant-software-pricing-pakistan-guide) covers the wider software budget.\n\n## Common POS price questions\n\n### Is hardware included in the published Restrova fee?\n\nHardware is a cost to confirm separately. Provide the device list and ask for an itemized scope. Do not interpret software pricing as a quotation for computers, printers, installation or supplies.\n\n### Is the lowest monthly fee the best value?\n\nOnly compare price after the essential tasks have been demonstrated. Include device changes, support, staff work and unresolved dependencies over the same period. Calculate variable fees month by month rather than relying on an annual sales average.\n\n### What should a useful POS quote contain?\n\nIt should identify the branches and channels, fee formula, setup work, devices, support arrangements, exclusions and acceptance tasks. Use the [POS buying checklist](/blog/how-to-choose-restaurant-pos-software-pakistan), then [request a free Restrova demo](/contact) with your menu, devices and a realistic closing scenario.",
